{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And those who camp on the east, toward the sunrise: the standard of the camp of Judah.</b> The reason for the arrangement of the standards according to this manner — the earlier authorities have already spoken of it, each according to his own understanding. And what seems close to me to say regarding this is that they are arranged according to four levels that encompass all human perfection: first the acquisition of wisdom, and after it the acquisition of character traits, and after that the acquisition of might, and after all of them the acquisition of wealth — for thus the Rambam arranged them, and our Rabbis of blessed memory said (Nedarim 38a): the Shekhinah does not rest except upon one who is wise, mighty, wealthy, and humble, for humility is the head of all character traits. Therefore these standards, which came for the resting of the Shekhinah among them — Scripture arranged them according to this manner, each man according to his own excellence, to tell you that these are worthy of having the Shekhinah rest upon them, for all four of these excellences were found in them." "Judah, Issachar, and Zebulun journey first, for from them Torah goes forth; therefore the doubling ״קֵדְמָה מִזְרָחָה״ is stated, to indicate that from them goes forth the light of Torah. For of Judah it is stated (Genesis 49:10): ״לֹא יָסוּר שֵׁבֶט מִיהוּדָה וּמְחֹקֵק מִבֵּין רַגְלָיו״ — these are the heads of the diaspora and the princes of the land of Israel (see Sanhedrin 5a there), and מְחֹקֵק means nothing but Torah, as it is stated of Moses (Deuteronomy 33:21): ״כִּי שָׁם חֶלְקַת מְחֹקֵק סָפוּן״, and it is written (Proverbs 31:5): ״פֶּן יִשְׁתֶּה וְיִשְׁכַּח מְחֻקָּק״. And camping with him is the tribe of Issachar, of whom it is stated (I Chronicles 12:32): ״וּמִבְּנֵי יִשָּׂשכָר יוֹדְעֵי בִינָה לַעִתִּים״. The tribe of Zebulun, of whom it is stated (Judges 5:14): ״וּמִזְּבוּלוּן מֹשְׁכִים בְּשֵׁבֶט סֹפֵר״. And furthermore, that he would sustain the hands of Issachar — and therefore it does not say ״וְעָלָיו מַטֵּה זְבוּלוּן״, because he did not wish to make him subordinate to the tribe of Issachar, to teach that the one who studies and the one who sustains the one who studies are equal. And of them it is stated ״רִאשׁוֹנָה יִסָּעוּ״, for theirs is the right of first place in war: for the wars of Israel are not waged with sword and spear but rather they must be חֲמוּשִׁים, armed — armed with the five books of the Torah, which are divided into seven books, which is the meaning of מְזֻיָּנִים, and it is included in the number twenty-seven letters, corresponding to the number of initial letters of יְהוּדָה יִשָּׂשכָר זְבוּלוּן — to tell you that the merit of Torah assists them in war, and they are the head of the standard, which signals victory." "The standard of the camp of Reuben, Simeon, and Gad — southward, which is called דָּרוֹם on account of דָּר רוֹם, 'dwells on high' — for the sun dwells at its height; so too all who are lowly by nature, HaShem ultimately raises up. And humility is the head of all good traits, and this trait was found in Reuben, for he confessed and was not ashamed regarding the matter of Bilhah, as our Rabbis of blessed memory said (see Sotah 7b): 'Who caused Reuben to confess…' — as Rashi brings in the portion of Ve-Zot Ha-Berakhah (33:7). And this is drawn from the trait of humility, for every haughty person is ashamed to acknowledge the truth. And from Simeon were teachers and scribes and poor people, among whom humility is found more than among the wealthy. And so Gad was a master of righteousness, as it is stated of him (Deuteronomy 33:21): ״צִדְקַת ה׳ עָשָׂה וּמִשְׁפָּטָיו עִם יִשְׂרָאֵל״ — meaning that his מִשְׁפָּטִים, that is, according to the line of strict justice, he did not need to go except עִם יִשְׂרָאֵל, not at the head of the vanguard; but on the side of righteousness he went before them, like the צִדְקַת ה׳ that goes before the camp of Israel. And lest you say that perhaps because of the haughtiness of their heart they went at the head — Scripture comes to teach (Genesis 49:19): ״גָּד גְּדוּד יְגוּדֶנּוּ וְהוּא יָגֵד עָקֵב״ — the גְּדוּד marched in humility like the עָקֵב, which signals the category of humility, as it is stated (Proverbs 22:4): ״עֵקֶב עֲנָוָה יִרְאַת ה׳״." "<b>The standard of the camp of Ephraim, Manasseh, and Benjamin — westward; and they shall journey third.</b> For the excellence of might is third, and it is written of them (Psalms 80:3): ״לִפְנֵי אֶפְרַיִם וּבִנְיָמִין וּמְנַשֶּׁה עוֹרְרָה אֶת גְּבוּרָתֶךָ״ etc. — for Joseph is the firstborn bull, who possesses strength and might, and Benjamin is a wolf that tears. And this acquisition goes and diminishes, for from day to day a person's strength fails from the side of the root moisture's seeping away, for the day of death begins from the day of birth. Therefore they camped toward the west wind, for in that direction the sun goes and wanes." "<b>The standard of the camp of Dan, Asher, and Naphtali — northward.</b> ״מֵאָשֵׁר שְׁמֵנָה לַחְמוֹ״ — from there gold comes forth, and all three of them were masters of wealth. For it is stated (Genesis 49:20): ״מֵאָשֵׁר שְׁמֵנָה לַחְמוֹ״, and it is written (Deuteronomy 33:23): ״נַפְתָּלִי שְׂבַע רָצוֹן וּמָלֵא בִּרְכַת ה׳״ — that is, it makes rich. And the tribe of Dan made golden calves on account of the abundance of gold that was showered upon them, and therefore he was the gatherer for all the camps. And this acquisition is the least of them all; therefore it is stated of them ״לָאַחֲרוֹנָה יִסְעוּ״. And the facing of all of them is toward the Shekhinah which is in the middle, for all of them together are good when one serves with them for the sake of Heaven. And Judah is head of a standard, for he is a king and is called a young lion; therefore it is his right to go first in war. And so Dan, a young lion, went last, for the essence of war is front and rear. And Reuben the firstborn is head of a standard, and so Ephraim is head of a standard, for Joseph was the firstborn."], :book :numbers, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {1 "The Kli Yakar plays on חֲמוּשִׁים ('armed') and חֲמִשָּׁה חֻמְשֵׁי תּוֹרָה ('five fifth-parts of Torah'), and on מְזֻיָּנִים ('armed') and מִזְּבוּלוּן מֹשְׁכִים בְּשֵׁבֶט סֹפֵר. The wordplay linking מְזֻיָּנִים to the שֵׁבֶט ('staff/tribe') of Zebulun the scribe is not fully explicit in the Hebrew but is operative in the punning logic.", 4 "The phrase ״מֵאָשֵׁר שְׁמֵנָה לַחְמוֹ״ is presented by the Kli Yakar as a prooftext both for Asher's wealth (Genesis 49:20) and as a springboard for 'from there gold comes forth,' which appears to be his own interpretive gloss linking 'oil/bread' to 'gold'; the transition is syntactically seamless and I have preserved it as written."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:40:29.387884395Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}